ages and faulty flashing attempts. Detection of the locked state triggers the \"Ultra-Fast WorldCup Hunting Mode\" that rapidly cycles `update.exe` calls at 48ms intervals to catch the `InUsbBurn` state after a user reset. This mode aims to unlock the device by flashing specific images to the environment partition, followed by resuming the flashing process automatically.\n\n\nThe persistent `PID_0D02` USB handle detection, even after reboots, suggested a stale device entry. A fast 900ms \"getvar\" ping was implemented to verify Fastboot's liveliness. Timeout responses now correctly indicate a dead USB handle, preventing the script from falsely detecting Fastboot.\n\nNon-ASCII characters causing mojibake were removed from the script and saved with UTF-8 with BOM to eliminate display issues.\n\n\nThe blocking `Read-Host` call in the original script caused watchdog resets due to the lack of USB traffic while waiting for user input. This has been replaced with a non-blocking `Read-ChoiceWithKeepAlive` function.\n\nThis new function polls for console input and, crucially, sends keep-alive Fastboot commands every two seconds to prevent the device from resetting due to the watchdog timeout during user input.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# ==============================================================================\\n# MOTOR PRINCIPAL: PROGRAMA PERFECTO XVIEW+ (ZTE ZXV10 B866V2 - S905X2 G12A)\\n# Fusion integral de todas las herramientas de la memoria USB + hallazgos REA\\n# Reglas absolutas:\\n#   1. 100% Externo (Cero tornillos, Cero TTL)\\n#   2. Proteccion total de factory.img (Widevine L1) y cri_data.img (MAC/Serie)\\n#   3. Salto directo del bloqueo QR RSA-2048 de ZTE mediante programas integrados\\n#      (WorldCup InUsbBurn 48ms VID_1B8E / Recovery fastbootd PID_4EE7 /\\n#       U-Boot Fastboot PID_0D02 / Llave QADEBUG.ini / ADB Directo)\\n# ==============================================================================\\n\\n[Conso